My first question is the one I always ask when I'm presented with
definitions: What is the purpose of these definitions?

Are they to guide science and technology or are they merely snapshots of
current thought expected to give insight into the progress of artificial
intelligence as a science and as a social event?  For the former they
are much too speculative.  For the latter they may have value, though
it is hard to see how current consensus is represented by them.  I
would doubt that these generations break the issues down according
to the proper criteria of advancement.  Nancy already raised one key issue:
that autonomy and self-organization will most likely far precede human
equivalence.  And what is the meaning of the distinction between generations
nine and ten, except the use of more laudatory pronous?

What are the sources or inspirations behind these definitions?

